rs the distinction of being the only divided capital in Europe, a symbolic representation of the island's tumultuous history. Established in antiquity, its roots can be traced back to the 7th century BC when it was known as Ledra, a city-state in the Kingdom of Cyprus. Over the centuries, Nicosia has witnessed the influences of various empires, including the Romans, Byzantines, and Ottomans, making it a melting pot of cultures and religions that reflect the complex tapestry of Mediterranean history.

